    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Genotype frequencies under random mating for genes with three alleles are shown in Figure 2.6. Here it is convenient to label the alleles as $ A_{1} $, $ A_{2} $, and $ A_{3} $ and the corresponding allele frequencies as $ p_{1} $, $ p_{2} $, and $ p_{3} $. Because there are only three alleles, $ p_{1} + p_{2} + p_{3} = 1 $. With three alleles there are six diploid genotypes, and under random mating their expected frequencies are as follows:",
