    {
      "type": "problem",
      "content": "PROBLEM 2.8 Four alleles of the gene Adh coding for alcohol dehydrogenase were found in a Texas population of Phlox cuspidata <sup>[400]</sup>. The alleles may be designated Adh-1, Adh-2, Adh-3, and Adh-4. Their frequencies were estimated as 0.11, 0.84, 0.01, and 0.04, respectively. What are the expected Hardy-Weinberg proportions of the 10 genotypes?",
